*pro.user


**/.vs/
build/
config.tests/*/.qmake.stash
config.tests/*/Makefile

# Staged installer payload and generated installer inputs. scripts\build-seathub.ps1 writes these
# from the deploy folder every run; they are build output, not sources.
installer/packages/*/data/
installer/packages/*/meta/license.txt
installer/config/seathub.ico

# Test build output. The suites are built in place (`qmake <suite>.pro && jom` inside tests/), so
# the generated Makefile, moc/object files, binaries and any `-o <suite>-out.txt` report land beside
# the sources. tests/ is entirely this fork's (upstream ships no test tree).
tests/Makefile
tests/.qmake.stash
tests/target_wrapper.bat
tests/*.obj
tests/*.exe
tests/*.moc
tests/moc_*
tests/qrc_*
tests/*-out.txt
# Plan 15: tst_telemetry.pro and tst_facade_wiring.pro both compile app/seathub/telemetry.cpp,
# each under its own DEFINES (tst_telemetry.pro alone widens acceptDsn() for its loopback-DSN
# tests) - the flat `tests/*.obj` pattern above left both projects sharing one `telemetry.obj` in
# the same directory, and a naive mtime-based incremental build (jom) had no way to tell that the
# object on disk was compiled under the OTHER project's flags, silently reusing a stale one and
# losing the loopback override. Each of the two suites' OBJECTS_DIR/MOC_DIR keeps its own.
tests/obj-*/
